Skip the byte swap in the _TIFFSwab*BitData() post-decode routines when the buffer size is not
a multiple of the sample size, instead of failing an assertion.

TIFFScanlineSize() of a contiguous YCbCr image divides the size of a row of sampling blocks by
the vertical subsampling, so with 1x4 subsampling and an odd width the scanline size is not a
multiple of the sample size (3 bytes for one 16-bit pixel). TIFFReadScanline() of such an image
in non-native byte order passes that size to _TIFFSwab16BitData() (likewise 24, 32 and 64 bits),
whose assert((cc & 1) == 0) aborts; tiff_read_rgba_fuzzer reads every scanline after
TIFFReadRGBAImage(), so a 164-byte uncompressed big-endian file aborts it. Includes
test/test_swab_odd_size.c.
Upstream: open issue libtiff/libtiff#669 (by Marsman1996, 2025-02-09) reports the same
_TIFFSwab16BitData assertion through tiffcmp; draft MR !695 (by Su_Laus, 2025-02-11, last
updated 2025-12-13) checks the post-decode length and errors out instead of skipping the swap.
Not fixed as of 7c72b091 (master HEAD on 2026-11-21).
Drop this patch once !695 lands.

diff --git a/libtiff/tif_read.c b/libtiff/tif_read.c
index ccb1a956..c61040ef 100644
--- a/libtiff/tif_read.c
+++ b/libtiff/tif_read.c
@@ -1797,27 +1797,31 @@ void _TIFFNoPostDecode(TIFF *tif, uint8_t *buf, tmsize_t cc)
 void _TIFFSwab16BitData(TIFF *tif, uint8_t *buf, tmsize_t cc)
 {
     (void)tif;
-    assert((cc & 1) == 0);
+    if ((cc & 1) != 0)
+        return;
     TIFFSwabArrayOfShort((uint16_t *)buf, cc / 2);
 }
 
 void _TIFFSwab24BitData(TIFF *tif, uint8_t *buf, tmsize_t cc)
 {
     (void)tif;
-    assert((cc % 3) == 0);
+    if (cc % 3 != 0)
+        return;
     TIFFSwabArrayOfTriples((uint8_t *)buf, cc / 3);
 }
 
 void _TIFFSwab32BitData(TIFF *tif, uint8_t *buf, tmsize_t cc)
 {
     (void)tif;
-    assert((cc & 3) == 0);
+    if ((cc & 3) != 0)
+        return;
     TIFFSwabArrayOfLong((uint32_t *)buf, cc / 4);
 }
 
 void _TIFFSwab64BitData(TIFF *tif, uint8_t *buf, tmsize_t cc)
 {
     (void)tif;
-    assert((cc & 7) == 0);
+    if ((cc & 7) != 0)
+        return;
     TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble((double *)buf, cc / 8);
 }
